                {
                    "file": "logger.hpp",
                    "line": 79,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Anwaar Hadi",
                        "email": "anwaar.hadi@ibm.com",
                        "username": "anwaarhadi"
                    },
                    "message": "When the lg2 call was written as lg2::error(message), the code failed to compile due to both logger.hpp and lg2 having a function named \"log\". The work-around was to specify the message as a key-value pair as seen in the update. I removed the comment to avoid further confusion."
                }
